  "title": "In filters, protocols may also be value_string references.",
  "description": "When filtering on e.g. \"smb2.cmd == find\", the filter is currently considered\ninvalid because (the unquoted) \"find\" is considered a protocol reference,\nrather than a string literal as in e.g. \"smb2.cmd == read\".\n\nFix can be tested on e.g. [this sample trace](https://wiki.wireshark.org/uploads/__moin_import__/attachments/SMB2/smb2-peter.pcap)",
