  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "45ce556b29503d5b242291c083cb95217426a8b5",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1572650783,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Thank you for your contribution but I'm strongly opposed to this kind of change.\n\n\"find\" is syntactically a protocol name and the meaning of the expression is clear (even if the comparison might be invalid). The syntax is not always perfect but this makes it worse. We should not try to guess or try to attribute some other meaning to this expression. There are already perfectly good ways to compare an integer to a value string using double quotes.\n\nThe solution here to to use double quotes for value strings, or propose some new syntax specific for value strings if you don't like that for some reason, that may or may not be accepted (probably not).\n\nSo much so that I intend to disallow value strings without quotes, even in cases where they might be working, to preemptively avoid this kind of solution and train users to say what they mean.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-09-22T14:09:18.322Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-09-22T14:09:18.322Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 252583532,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 12211,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "9af3d289c289080e27fd377525c459165d1a74e2",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1572767895,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Thanks for looking at it.\n\nEnforcing quoted strings would certainly avoid any confusion on why \"smb2.cmd == read\"\nis OK, but \"smb2.cmd == find\" is not (which, I see, is much better explained in master\nthan 4.0.8). Would break some habits, I'm sure, but it certainly is clearer.\n\nIn my view also less convenient, but I'm biased by using this kind of syntax a lot.",
          "author": {
            "id": 13889755,
            "username": "prebeng",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "Preben Guldberg",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3ea14473e4af4540823839d0288d8c97808145c93f7909dd0acb19e50e1055cd?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/prebeng"
          },
